,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,-3.576278118089249e-07,0.0,0.0,0.0,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,0.0,0.0,0.0,-0.000940714729949832,-0.0018435402307659388,-7.152555099310121e-07],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,32,21495,57960,55114,19360,3,448,57960,4044,362,284,220,16,19,24884,43298,3,374,1640,17433,304,264,12671,1380,400,1867,3,374,264,23033,13,2585,1657,12348,525,304,57960,4044,425,3,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nA triangle $\\triangle ABC$ with $\\angle A = 14^\\circ$ is inscribed in a circle where $AB$ is a diameter. How many degrees are in $\\angle B$?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"9c85c994204f5fb804af9963a937603ae2b7541fe1380b71ef1780f16cfa70f2"},"seconds":7.040549039840698,"seed":731127484411193743,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to use the properties of circles and triangles, specifically the fact that the angle subtended by a diameter in a semicircle is a right angle.\n\nGiven:\n- \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is inscribed in a circle.\n- \\(AB\\) is the diameter of the circle.\n- \\(\\angle A = 14^\\circ\\).\n\nSince \\(AB\\) is the diameter, \\(\\angle ACB\\) (the angle subtended by the diameter) is a right angle, i.e., \\(\\angle ACB = 90^\\circ\\).\n\nIn any triangle, the sum of the interior angles is \\(180^\\circ\\). Therefore, for \\(\\triangle ABC\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\angle A + \\angle B + \\angle ACB = 180^\\circ.\n\\]\nSubstituting the known values:\n\\[\n14^\\circ + \\angle B + 90^\\circ = 180^\\circ.\n\\]\nSimplifying the equation:\n\\[\n104^\\circ + \\angle B = 180^\\circ.\n\\]\nSubtracting \\(104^\\circ\\) from both sides:\n\\[\n\\angle B = 76^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle B\\) is \\(\\boxed{76}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{76}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"geometry:181"}
